  "notes": "West leads the ♦J against 4♠. West's diamond lead goes to East's ♦A. East switches to a heart, won in dummy. South should cash the ♠A and ♠K. The 4-1 trump split turns an easy hand into a difficult one.\n\nAs West has 2 certain trump tricks, South must avoid a heart loser. The only hope is to take 4 club tricks, discarding dummy's ♥2 on the last round. South's heart loser can then be ruffed in dummy.\n\nFor this plan to work, West must follow to all 4 rounds of clubs. Since West must have length in clubs, he should be played for the ♣J. South should lead the ♣9 or ♣10 and pass it when West follows low.\n\nIf West has the hoped for distribution, there is nothing he can do. South plays 3 more rounds of clubs discarding dummy's ♥2 on the last round. South can now ruff his heart loser in the dummy and concede 2 trump tricks.",
